// CORE VOCABULARY — the bulk of the word list, in a compact shape.
//
// The original 70 entries in vocabulary.js are "deep": usage essay,
// collocations, a mini-dialogue, a speaking prompt, a review question. That
// depth is right for the highest-value expressions, but it does not scale to a
// thousand words without the quality collapsing.
//
// So these are dictionary-style: the word, what it means, a register label, a
// short example sentence, and a usage note wherever Mexican usage actually
// differs from what a textbook would tell you. Pronunciation is generated from
// the spelling by spanishIPA, which is verified against all 70 hand-written
// transcriptions.
//
// Ordered by the tutor spec's FREQUENCY PRIORITY: the things you need to say
// first come first.
//
//   w   = the word, with its article where that matters (el/la teaches gender)
//   en  = English meaning
//   cat = category, used by the filter chips in Learn
//   reg = "formal" | "informal" | "slang"; omitted means neutral
//   ex  = [Spanish example, English translation]
//   note = Mexican usage note, only where it earns its place

